The consolidated review explicitly flags some issues as “fatal,” but per the calibration set many “fatal” labels in text correspond to major, not acceptance-killing, flaws when the underlying work is solid and fixable in a revision. Here, the core technical contributions (dataset, graphs, baseline implementation) remain valid; the over-claiming about repository-level reasoning and competitiveness vs. LLMs does not make the submission “not even a paper” or undermine all central results.

