**Positioning on the calibration scale:**

- Clearly above the 0.0 diffusion augmentation paper: KARMA does not have a completely unvalidated central claim; it has real empirical work and a coherent conceptual framework.
- Weaker and more internally inconsistent than TempFlow-GRPO (7.5) and World-In-World (7.0), which, despite some overclaiming, have clearly specified algorithms and better-aligned theory/experiments.
- On par or slightly below PBRR (5.0) and VideoZoomer (5.5) in total quality; unlike those, KARMA has *fatal-level* issues in its core theoretical narrative and algorithm specification, even though its empirical breadth is decent.

Given this, KARMA belongs in a **clear reject but not catastrophic** band: substantially better than 0–2 “not a paper” territory, but below the ~5 borderline-accept region due to fundamental issues with theoretical claims and under-specified core mechanisms.

