- The counterfactual labeling is real and materially strengthens the evidence. The paper describes stricter counterfactual tests for both in-context and RM loopholes (lines 239–242, 486–488, 638–639), so the review is right that the supervision is unusually strong for this kind of safety problem.
- The results really do go beyond one easy setup: there are response-level detection results, dataset-level deployment-style setups, and partial-loophole training (lines 623–787). The loophole-discovery case study is also genuinely present rather than decorative (lines 790–883).

The main weaknesses in the review are also real:

