On empirical support, the review is again fair. The results are competitive, but the paper overclaims. Table 1 shows Omni slightly behind FastText on average Spearman but best on average Kendall (lines 405–456). Table 2 shows Omni near Word2Vec/ELMo and above BERT under this setup, but the margin is small and the setup is unusual (lines 470–525). Table 3 shows best average ARI but not best NMI (lines 531–540, 966–972). So “competitive with some wins” is accurate; “often surpasses mainstream models” is overstated.

