| **Technical soundness** | Solid on the systems side; the ASPS/CASPS metrics are well-defined. The Waymax comparison has a meaningful gap (OOM without hardware specification). Bicycle model is standard. No statistical testing of training results. |
| **Empirical support** | Mixed: the throughput claims are credible and well-demonstrated. However, the 95% goal-reaching rate is on training scenarios only (no test split), collision rates are not reported despite safety-critical framing, and multi-agent coordination experiments are absent. |
| **Significance** | High potential significance — enabling billion-step multi-agent driving research previously infeasible. But the positioning overpromises (million FPS headline vs. ~200K CASPS; "multi-agent learning" framing vs. independent PPO experiments only). |
